@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Take a screen capture
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Person diagnosing" as person
box "Frontend — Ride app (components library)" #E0F2FE
  participant "DiagnosticPanel" as panel
end box
box "Frontend — Ride app (ride application)" #E0F2FE
  participant "DiagnosticsHost" as host
end box
box "Frontend — Ride app (domain library)" #ECFDF3
  participant "BrowserScreenCapture" as capture
  participant "DiagnosticRecorder" as recorder
end box
box "Device — Browser" #F2F4F7
  participant "navigator.mediaDevices" as media
end box
person -> panel : Press Capture screen
panel -> host : capture output
host -> host : Close the dialog; the mark reads "Capturing…"; wait two animation frames
host -> capture : SCREEN_CAPTURE.capture()
capture -> media : getDisplayMedia with preferCurrentTab
media -> person : Ask the browser's own permission to share the tab
alt the person allows it
  person --> media : Share this tab
  media --> capture : Stream with one video track
  capture -> capture : Play the stream in a detached video element
  capture -> capture : Draw the first frame to a canvas; encode a PNG
  capture -> media : Clear the timer; stop each track; let go of the video element (L2-178 AC13, AC20)
  capture --> host : CapturedScreen: picture, width, height
  host -> recorder : keepCapture(captured)
  recorder -> recorder : Number and name it; add one CAP line; past 8, drop the oldest and add a CAP line that names it (L2-178 AC9, AC13)
  recorder --> host : 1
  host -> host : showModal()
  host -> panel : Status "Screen capture 1 kept"
else the person refuses, or the capture fails
  media --> capture : Reject with NotAllowedError, or a stream that gives no frame in 5 s
  capture -> media : Stop each track that was opened (L2-178 AC20)
  capture --> host : Reject with ScreenCaptureError, code refused or failed
  host -> recorder : captureFailed(code, the error's message)
  recorder -> recorder : Add one CAP line: the code and the error as quoted text (L2-178 AC14)
  host -> host : showModal()
  host -> panel : Status "The browser didn’t share the screen, so no capture was kept. The ride carries on."
end
panel --> person : Show the status in the dialog
note over panel, recorder : The ride, the bike and the recording carry on throughout (L2-178 AC14)
note over panel, host : Without the Screen Capture API, canCapture is false and Capture screen is off (L2-178 AC14)
@enduml
